{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And it produced blossoms.</b> As it sounds." "<b>Bud.</b> It is the setting of the fruit, when the blossom falls." "<b>And it yielded almonds.</b> When the fruit was recognized, it was recognized that they were almonds — like ״וַיִּגְדַּל הַיֶּלֶד וַיִּגָּמַל״ (Genesis 21); and this term is found with the fruit of the tree, as in ״וּבֹסֶר גֹּמֵל יִהְיֶה נִצָּה״ (Isaiah 18). And why almonds? It is the fruit that hastens to blossom before all other fruits — so too whoever stirs up dissension against the priesthood, his punishment hastens to come, as we find in Uzziah: ״וְהַצָּרַעַת זָרְחָה בְמִצְחוֹ״ (II Chronicles 26). Its Targum: ״וְכָפִית שִׁגְדִין״ — a kind of cluster of almonds bound together, these upon these."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:26.475312726Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}